# FlyRank Frontend Capstone Rules

## Technology Stack
- HTML5, CSS3, and JavaScript
- Node.js LTS and npm
- Git and GitHub
- Cursor AI
- React only when required by the project

## Coding Conventions
- Write clean, readable, maintainable code.
- Use semantic HTML and accessible components.
- Follow responsive, mobile-friendly design principles.
- Use clear and consistent file and variable names.
- Avoid unnecessary dependencies and features.
- Keep code organized and reusable.

## AI Development Guidelines
- Understand requirements before writing code.
- Explain important technical decisions.
- Do not invent test results or functionality.
- Review and test AI-generated code.
- Ask for clarification when necessary.
- Never expose passwords, API keys, or secrets.

## Git Conventions
- Follow Conventional Commits.
- Use prefixes such as feat:, fix:, docs:, and chore:.
- Keep commits focused and descriptive.

## Project Goal
Build a professional frontend capstone through
responsible AI-assisted development.
